<<~ kanawai "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/ref/RFC-2119">>

<<~ ahu #/head>>

! K17-R ~ one lease law on the realm boards

Wave C made a PersonaGroup's lease epoch rise only on a signed advance (`lease-advance`, `lares persona lease`) and built the fleet board's signed frontier. K17-R extends both laws to the Nexus and cabal-realm boards, as its own lane cut after Wave C lands (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane">>). It shares only the readers Wave C built: `hand-lineage`, the quorum act and `readWideningFrontier`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-mandate>>

!! The mandate (operator rulings on forks 3 and 4, 2026-10-22)

* ''One lease law.'' Every lease epoch rises only on a signed advance. A face advances by a per-writer signed slot under its KEL lineage. A Nexus or cabal-realm advance signs as a `QuorumAct` at the roster's threshold under its own epoch's lineage.
* ''The unsigned max-register retires entirely'' (`effectiveLeaseEpoch`, `rollLeaseEpochOnBoard`, with their fixtures); the signed path stands alone.
* ''The realm boards' frontiers widen K17 the same way the fleet board's do.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-slices>>

!! The five slices, one lane landed whole

# ''R1 ~ the mesh format.'' A quorum-lease slot, its writer and its reader under a charter lineage (`makeHandLineage` bound to the seal-epoch chain; an older epoch's keys come from the seal-roll chain).
# ''R2 ~ the writer on held seats.'' The `nexus-rekey` writer moves from the vessel's atom to a store-door row that signs at held seats, as `lares edge kapae --quorum` does.
# ''R3 ~ the readers.'' The herm's raise door (`effectiveLeaseEpochOnBoard`), `cabal-join`, the vessel standing and the realm clock read signed advances only.
# ''R4 ~ the retirement.'' The unsigned max-register leaves, and its fixtures migrate to signed fixtures through the real founding path.
# ''R5 ~ the realm boards' frontiers.'' The charter quorum hand signs its stream's frontier; the realm boards' readers (`memberAside`, `standsInRealm`, the vouch edges) widen only as of a qualifying frontier.

Red: an unsigned `rollLeaseEpochOnBoard` advance on a realm raises nothing, a sub-threshold hand raises nothing, and a threshold hand raises it.

<<~/ahu>>

